UPSTREAM SOURCES

  School spending, staffing, assets, attendance and retention
    Based on Steering Committee for the Review of Government Service Provision data, Report on Government Services
    2026, Part B section 4 School education (Productivity Commission). Licensed under CC BY 4.0, with the exception
    of the Commonwealth Coat of Arms and content supplied by third parties.
    https://www.pc.gov.au/ongoing/report-on-government-services
    Changes: reshaped to one row per state, year and measure; NSW and SA kept, Victoria and Australia as reference.

  NAPLAN results
    Australian Curriculum, Assessment and Reporting Authority (ACARA), NAPLAN national results 2008 to 2022 and
    2023 to 2026. Licensed under CC BY 4.0. https://www.acara.edu.au/contact-us/copyright
    Results before and after 2023 are on different scales and are kept apart. All school sectors. The NAP and ACARA
    logos are not used.

  Budget papers
    NSW Treasury, NSW Budget 2025-26 and 2026-27 (CC BY 4.0). Government of South Australia, 2026-27 Budget Paper 4
    Agency Statements (CC BY 4.0). State of Victoria, Department of Treasury and Finance, 2026-27 Department
    Performance Statement (CC BY 4.0). Australian Government Department of Education and National School Resourcing
    Board, Better and Fairer Schools Agreement progress report and section 22A review (CC BY 4.0). Cited for totals
    and shares; figures nominal.

  NSW school data
    NSW Department of Education (Centre for Education Statistics and Evaluation), data.nsw.gov.au. Licensed under
    Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY), as stated on each dataset page.
    - NSW public schools master dataset (school code, name, location, type, ICSEA)
    - NSW government school enrolments by head count (2015 to 2024 used)
    - NSW public schools Resource Allocation Model (RAM) funding by school, 2024 after adjustments
    Changes: reshaped to one row per school per year; contact columns removed. ICSEA is ACARA's index as republished
    by NSW in the master dataset. ICSEA and RAM are shown in the NSW view only: no SA equivalent is published.

  SA school data
    Department for Education, Government of South Australia, data.sa.gov.au. Licensed under CC BY 4.0.
    - SA government enrolments by school (Term 3 FTE, 2015 to 2024 used)
    - SA government preschool and school sites 2023 (points used to pick each school's polygon)
    Changes: a school renamed between years has one row per name under one school number; the years are added up by
    school number.

  NSW cadastre and aerial imagery
    © State of New South Wales (Spatial Services, a business unit of the Department of Customer Service NSW).
    Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia (CC BY 3.0 AU),
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/
    - NSW Cadastre: the inner Sydney outlines are unions of the cadastre lots picked for each school in Plotlay.
    - NSW Imagery: 5 outlines where two schools share one lot were drawn over it. No imagery tiles are included.

  SA land use
    SA Land Use Generalised 2025, Department for Housing and Urban Development, Government of South Australia,
    data.sa.gov.au/data/dataset/land-use-generalised. The data.sa.gov.au record states CC BY 4.0; the download's
    License.txt states Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia (CC BY 3.0 AU). The inner Adelaide outlines are the
    EDUCATION polygons under each school's point, used as released (dissolved valuation parcels); individual lots are
    not reconstructed.

  City of Adelaide parcels
    Property Boundaries, City of Adelaide, data.sa.gov.au/data/dataset/property-boundaries. Licensed under CC BY 4.0.
    Used for Gilles Street Primary School (the four parcels that name it).

  DEW rasters
    Metropolitan Adelaide 2022 green space and building rasters (0.5 m), Department for Environment and Water,
    Government of South Australia. Licensed under CC BY 4.0 ("AusGOAL CC BY (Attribution)"). Used to draw two edges
    of the Unley High School outline, where one land-use polygon also holds Urrbrae Agricultural High, TAFE SA and
    Waite land. No raster data is included.

NOT INCLUDED
  Nothing in this repository is derived from OpenStreetMap. No Google, Nearmap, Esri or Mapbox imagery was used.
  The SA cadastre and Location SA imagery were not used (they are not open data). ACARA's School Profile, School
  Location and My School content (per-school ICSEA for SA, per-school finance, per-school NAPLAN) are not used.
  No coat of arms or agency logo is used, and nothing here implies endorsement by any of these agencies.

